  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Copper for Development Campaign</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intended outcomes/results of this intervention are to advocate for policy reform on Mineral Revenue Management aimed at ringfencing mining revenues for spending/allocation to priority sectors (agriculture, health, energy, education) key to the improved socio -economic status of all citizens. The project has been implemented at two levels with a phased approach including the first part, which was a comprehensive research to understand the context on Zambia&apos;s extraction of the copper resource and use of revenue resources, and the second part being the campaign. The rationale for this was for the findings of the research to drive and propel the &#x2018;copper for development&apos; campaign.   The extension of the Copper for Development campaign is intended to implement actions on basis of commitments made for mineral revenue policy reform in Zambia&apos;s past general elections.</narrative>
  </description>
